WEBVTT

00:00:00.361 --> 00:00:03.293
Last video ended here: the integral of two

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.100
x plus one, all squared.

00:00:05.785 --> 00:00:06.535
Expanding works.

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:09.103
It's four x squared, plus four x, plus

00:00:09.224 --> 00:00:11.905
one, which integrates term by term to four

00:00:12.006 --> 00:00:14.566
x cubed over three, plus two x squared,

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:16.107
plus x, plus C.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.438
But look at this jar of sourdough starter.

00:00:20.121 --> 00:00:22.548
t hours after it's fed, it rises at

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.896
three, over the square root of four t

00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.621
plus one, centimetres per hour.

00:00:27.204 --> 00:00:29.452
Fast at first, then slower and slower.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.104
That rate has nothing to expand.

00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:34.773
So how far does it rise in six

00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:35.114
hours?

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:38.468
And how can algebra, and the chain rule

00:00:38.529 --> 00:00:40.697
run backwards, find primitives like these?

00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:42.503
First, the algebra.

00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:45.356
The power rule works on powers of x,

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.608
so rewrite the function as powers before integrating.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.586
One over x cubed is x to the

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:52.209
minus three.

00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:55.519
Raise the power to minus two, and divide

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.241
by minus two.

00:00:56.944 --> 00:01:00.093
That's minus one over two x squared, plus

00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:02.581
C on each side of zero, since x

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.504
can't be zero.

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:06.811
x to the three on two becomes x

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:07.874
to the five on two,

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:09.758
divided by five on two.

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:12.708
That's two fifths of x to the five

00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:14.896
on two, which needs x to be zero

00:01:15.058 --> 00:01:15.539
or positive.

00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:19.431
And a fraction like x cubed plus two

00:01:19.592 --> 00:01:22.300
x, all over x, splits into x squared

00:01:22.421 --> 00:01:23.022
plus two.

00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:26.615
Its primitive is x cubed over three, plus

00:01:26.657 --> 00:01:28.784
two x, plus C on each side of

00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:29.145
zero.

00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:30.584
Now the bracket.

00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:33.390
Treat it like x, and guess two x

00:01:33.431 --> 00:01:35.395
plus one, cubed, over three.

00:01:36.377 --> 00:01:38.177
Check by differentiating with the chain rule:

00:01:39.019 --> 00:01:42.799
differentiate the outside, keep the inside, then multiply

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.901
by the derivative of the inside, which is

00:01:44.942 --> 00:01:45.141
two.

00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:48.535
So the guess differentiates to two times the

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:49.580
bracket squared.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.372
Watch its gradient.

00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:54.570
It traces a curve exactly twice as high

00:01:54.671 --> 00:01:55.394
as the one we want.

00:01:56.099 --> 00:01:57.085
So halve the guess.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.959
Two x plus one, cubed, over six, differentiates

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.548
to exactly two x plus one, squared.

00:02:04.554 --> 00:02:07.129
Dividing by the inside's rate is the reverse

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:07.612
chain rule.

00:02:08.115 --> 00:02:10.544
But expanding gave a different-looking answer.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:11.940
Which one is right?

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:13.805
Expand the bracket answer.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.376
It's four x cubed over three, plus two

00:02:17.477 --> 00:02:20.263
x squared, plus x, plus one sixth.

00:02:20.865 --> 00:02:23.262
That's the expanded answer, plus one sixth.

00:02:24.108 --> 00:02:26.194
On the graph, they're the same shape, a

00:02:26.296 --> 00:02:27.339
constant gap apart.

00:02:27.942 --> 00:02:30.510
So both are primitives, and the C absorbs

00:02:30.531 --> 00:02:30.951
the difference.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.538
This works for any bracket a x plus

00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:33.659
b.

00:02:34.422 --> 00:02:36.684
Differentiating a x plus b, to the n

00:02:36.704 --> 00:02:39.927
plus one, multiplies by n plus one, and

00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:41.208
by the inner rate, a.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.605
So the primitive divides by both.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.292
The integral of a x plus b, to

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.434
the n, is a x plus b to

00:02:48.454 --> 00:02:49.214
the n plus one,

00:02:49.715 --> 00:02:52.497
over a times n plus one, plus C,

00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:55.700
for a not zero and n not minus

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:55.900
one.

00:02:56.504 --> 00:02:57.294
Now the starter.

00:02:58.302 --> 00:03:00.269
Three over the root of four t plus

00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:00.550
one

00:03:01.071 --> 00:03:03.720
is three, times four t plus one to

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.763
the minus a half.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:06.861
Raise the power to a half.

00:03:07.385 --> 00:03:09.575
Then divide by the new power, a half,

00:03:10.118 --> 00:03:11.685
and by the inner rate, four.

00:03:12.588 --> 00:03:14.111
Three over two is one and a half,

00:03:14.592 --> 00:03:16.155
so the rise is one and a half

00:03:16.235 --> 00:03:18.479
times the root of four t plus one,

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:19.261
plus C.

00:03:20.384 --> 00:03:22.068
At t equals zero it hasn't risen yet,

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.195
so one and a half, plus C, is

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.502
zero, and C is minus one and a

00:03:26.563 --> 00:03:26.803
half.

00:03:27.787 --> 00:03:30.014
After six hours, the root of twenty-five is

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:30.515
five.

00:03:31.158 --> 00:03:32.684
So it has risen seven and a half,

00:03:32.866 --> 00:03:34.674
minus one and a half, which is six

00:03:34.816 --> 00:03:35.357
centimetres.

00:03:35.895 --> 00:03:38.163
The same idea works when the inside isn't

00:03:38.244 --> 00:03:40.713
linear, as long as the inside's derivative is

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:40.914
there.

00:03:41.778 --> 00:03:44.083
Find the integral of two x, times x

00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:45.626
squared plus one, cubed.

00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:48.427
The inside is x squared plus one.

00:03:48.992 --> 00:03:52.048
Its derivative, two x, is already sitting outside.

00:03:52.813 --> 00:03:54.723
So guess x squared plus one, to the

00:03:54.805 --> 00:03:55.910
four, over four.

00:03:56.716 --> 00:04:00.010
Differentiating gives four times the bracket cubed, times

00:04:00.111 --> 00:04:01.216
two x, over four.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.033
That's two x, times the bracket cubed, exactly

00:04:05.074 --> 00:04:05.636
the integrand.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.161
In general, the integral of u to the

00:04:08.362 --> 00:04:10.645
n, times d u by d x, is

00:04:10.846 --> 00:04:12.708
u to the n plus one, over n

00:04:12.729 --> 00:04:15.632
plus one, plus C, for n not minus

00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:15.832
one.

00:04:16.516 --> 00:04:19.012
What if the outside factor is just x?

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:22.142
The integral of x, times x squared plus

00:04:22.183 --> 00:04:23.004
one, cubed.

00:04:23.887 --> 00:04:26.528
Here x is half of two x, so

00:04:26.569 --> 00:04:28.109
the answer is half the last one:

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.751
x squared plus one, to the four, over

00:04:30.912 --> 00:04:31.091
eight.

00:04:32.176 --> 00:04:34.343
A missing number can be fixed, because a

00:04:34.404 --> 00:04:36.291
constant moves through the integral sign.

00:04:36.974 --> 00:04:39.182
But with no x outside at all, the

00:04:39.223 --> 00:04:41.932
integral of x squared plus one, cubed, can't

00:04:41.973 --> 00:04:42.675
be done this way.

00:04:43.358 --> 00:04:45.823
Two x isn't a constant, so dividing by

00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:47.347
it doesn't undo the chain rule.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:48.510
Check it:

00:04:49.173 --> 00:04:51.176
at x equals one, the derivative of that

00:04:51.238 --> 00:04:52.961
guess is six, not eight.

00:04:53.824 --> 00:04:54.045
Here,

00:04:54.588 --> 00:04:55.432
expand instead.

00:04:56.177 --> 00:04:58.311
One more worked example, with a root.

00:04:58.936 --> 00:05:00.200
Find the integral of

00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:03.131
x, over the square root of x squared

00:05:03.193 --> 00:05:03.794
plus four.

00:05:04.478 --> 00:05:07.389
First, rewrite it as x, times x squared

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.056
plus four, to the minus a half.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.753
The inside is x squared plus four, with

00:05:12.795 --> 00:05:13.839
derivative two x.

00:05:14.482 --> 00:05:16.266
We have x, which is half of that,

00:05:16.628 --> 00:05:17.730
so it's a missing number.

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:21.261
Raising the power to a half and dividing

00:05:21.302 --> 00:05:22.545
by a half doubles it:

00:05:23.228 --> 00:05:25.273
two times the square root of x squared

00:05:25.415 --> 00:05:25.996
plus four.

00:05:26.703 --> 00:05:27.711
Then take half of that.

00:05:28.739 --> 00:05:30.746
The answer is the square root of x

00:05:31.109 --> 00:05:32.955
squared plus four, plus C.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:33.839
And

00:05:34.362 --> 00:05:36.792
x squared plus four is always positive, so

00:05:36.914 --> 00:05:38.480
this works for every real x.

00:05:39.363 --> 00:05:42.650
Differentiating back gives x over the root, the

00:05:42.711 --> 00:05:43.732
integrand exactly.

00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:45.995
Here's a rule of thumb for the reverse

00:05:46.036 --> 00:05:46.457
chain rule.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.263
Fix a missing number, never a missing x.

00:05:51.005 --> 00:05:52.907
If the inside's derivative is out by a

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:54.649
constant, adjust the constant.

00:05:55.211 --> 00:05:56.797
If it needs an x that isn't there,

00:05:57.481 --> 00:05:58.505
use algebra instead.

00:06:01.296 --> 00:06:01.785
Your turn.

00:06:02.431 --> 00:06:05.078
Find the integral of six, over two x

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:07.827
plus one, to the four, for x not

00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:08.970
equal to minus a half.

00:06:09.615 --> 00:06:10.460
Pause here to answer.

00:06:21.635 --> 00:06:23.845
Rewrite it as six times two x plus

00:06:24.027 --> 00:06:25.213
one, to the minus four.

00:06:25.957 --> 00:06:28.258
Raise the power to minus three, then divide

00:06:28.299 --> 00:06:29.039
by minus three,

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.220
and by the inner rate, two.

00:06:32.104 --> 00:06:34.182
Six over minus six is minus one.

00:06:34.945 --> 00:06:37.326
So the answer is minus one over two

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.328
x plus one, cubed, plus C.

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:42.450
Forgetting the two gives minus two over the

00:06:42.491 --> 00:06:45.613
bracket cubed, which differentiates to twice the integrand.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.468
Last one.

00:06:48.076 --> 00:06:51.403
Find the integral of x squared, times x

00:06:51.484 --> 00:06:53.708
cubed plus one, to the four.

00:06:54.436 --> 00:06:55.268
Pause here to answer.

00:07:05.881 --> 00:07:08.051
The inside is x cubed plus one,

00:07:08.633 --> 00:07:10.581
and its derivative is three x squared.

00:07:11.244 --> 00:07:13.457
We have x squared, which is a third

00:07:13.477 --> 00:07:14.865
of that: a missing number.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.196
So the answer is a third of x

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.988
cubed plus one, to the five, over five.

00:07:20.771 --> 00:07:22.737
That's x cubed plus one, to the five,

00:07:22.918 --> 00:07:24.683
over fifteen, plus C.

00:07:25.808 --> 00:07:28.816
Integrating the two factors separately and multiplying doesn't

00:07:28.937 --> 00:07:29.217
work.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.977
A product doesn't integrate factor by factor.

00:07:33.614 --> 00:07:35.856
So algebra turns a function into powers,

00:07:36.378 --> 00:07:38.459
and the reverse chain rule divides by the

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.121
rate of a linear inside.

00:07:40.984 --> 00:07:43.432
Next, an exponential: the integral of e

00:07:43.975 --> 00:07:44.777
to the three x.

00:07:45.461 --> 00:07:47.431
Does the same division by three appear?

00:07:50.121 --> 00:07:51.005
Here are the key notes.

00:07:51.527 --> 00:07:53.296
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:53.316 --> 00:07:53.798
to copy them.
